# LeakSanitizer findings in third_party/llama.cpp, which this project does not patch (AGENTS.md hard
# rule 1). Each line names one upstream site and why it is here; a leak whose stack starts in our own
# code gets no entry - it is a bug to fix, not to suppress.

# The loopback rpc-server gate G16 registers lives as long as the process: its thread serves until
# exit (it has no stop call), and the CPU backend it serves from is never freed.
leak:ggml_backend_rpc_start_server
# The RPC registry and device that ggml_backend_rpc_add_server creates, and the buffer type a device
# hands out (ggml_backend_rpc_buffer_type), are process-lifetime objects upstream never frees.
leak:ggml_backend_rpc_add_server
leak:ggml_backend_rpc_buffer_type
